# The repository is stored with LF line endings (that is what every commit through HEAD
# contains). Windows editors and tooling had rewritten the entire working tree to CRLF, which
# made `git status` report all 72 tracked files as modified with 9,391 insertions and 9,391
# deletions -- every line of every file "changed", with no actual content difference. That churn
# would have buried real work in an unreviewable diff.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` normalizes text files to LF in the index regardless of what the working
# tree holds, so the same thing cannot happen again. After adding this file, run once:
#
#     git add --renormalize .
#
# ...which rewrites the index using these rules and drops the phantom diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be normalized -- doing so corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary

# PowerShell tooling under tools/ is executed by Windows PowerShell and is kept CRLF on checkout.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
